 "そこいら": "[around there ; that area]\nمثال: 今日、野球の試合を見に行くと、売り子がお湯の入ったタンクを持って、そこいらを歩き回っている。\n→ If you go to a baseball game today, sellers are walking around with hot-water tanks. / لِكَيْ, أَنْ (Introducing a subordinate clause that expresses an aim, purpose, or goal (“final) / ذٰلِكَ, ذَاكَ (The (thing, person, idea, etc) indicated or understood from context, especially ) / ذَاكَ (that thing) / ذٰلِكَ (that thing) / تِلْكَ (that thing) / اَلَّذِي (which) / اَلَّتِي (which) / اَلَّذِينَ (which)  [that] / فَـ, لِذَا (As a result; for that reason; therefore; because of this; due to this.) / إِذًا, فَ (Used after a pause for thought to introduce a new topic, question or story, or a)  [(or) so]\nafter a quantity, usu. as ...かそこいら or ...やそこいら",
