 "それが": "لِكَيْ, أَنْ (Introducing a subordinate clause that expresses an aim, purpose, or goal (“final) / ذٰلِكَ, ذَاكَ (The (thing, person, idea, etc) indicated or understood from context, especially ) / ذَاكَ (that thing) / ذٰلِكَ (that thing) / تِلْكَ (that thing) / اَلَّذِي (which) / اَلَّتِي (which) / اَلَّذِينَ (which)  [that]\nsubject of sentence / [well, actually ... ; well, unfortunately ...]\nused to respond hesitantly to a question",
 "それがし": "أَحَد (One or some person of unspecified or indefinite identity.)  [someone] / أَي, إِي (The name of the Latin script letter I/i.)  [I]\nused by samurai",
 "それきた": "فَهِمْتَ, فَهِمْتِ (Do you understand?) / فَهِمْتُ (I understand.)  [got it]",
 "それこそ": "خُصُوصًا, خَاصَّةً (Particularly; to a greater extent than is normal.)  [especially] / بِالتَّأْكِيد (Certainly, undoubtedly.)  [surely] / كَأَنَّ, كَأَنَّمَا (As though; in a manner suggesting.)  [as if]",
 "それしき": "تافِه (Ignorable; of little significance or value.)  [trivial]",
 "それしゃ": "خَبِير, مَاهِر (Extraordinary capable or knowledgeable.) / مُتَخَصِّص, مُتَخَصِّصَة (A person with extensive knowledge or ability in a given subject.)  [expert] / غَيْشَا (A Japanese female entertainer skilled in various arts such as tea ceremony, danc)  [geisha]",
 "それじしん": "نَفْسُهُ, نَفْسُهَا (it; used to intensify the subject, especially to emphasize that it is the only p)  [itself]",
 "それじたい": "لذاته وعينه (Inherently; viewed independently, without reference to anything else.)  [in itself]\nمثال: お金それ自体は何の意味もないものだ。\n→ Money, as such, has no meaning.",
 "それじゃ": "[well, ... ; right, ...]\nused to end a conversation or introduce a remark\nمثال: それじゃあこのメモを渡してください。緊急です。\n→ Then, please give him this note. This is urgent. / فَـ, لِذَا (As a result; for that reason; therefore; because of this; due to this.) / إِذًا, فَ (Used after a pause for thought to introduce a new topic, question or story, or a)  [so] / [that way (would mean ...) ; if that is the case] / [bye then]",
 "それじゃあ": "[well, ... ; right, ...]\nused to end a conversation or introduce a remark\nمثال: それじゃあこのメモを渡してください。緊急です。\n→ Then, please give him this note. This is urgent. / فَـ, لِذَا (As a result; for that reason; therefore; because of this; due to this.) / إِذًا, فَ (Used after a pause for thought to introduce a new topic, question or story, or a)  [so] / [that way (would mean ...) ; if that is the case] / [bye then]",
 "それそうおう": "مُنَاسِب (Suitable or fit; proper; felicitous.) / لَائِق (Suitable to the social situation or to social respect or social discreetness; so)  [appropriate]",
 "それそれ": "[come on ; hurry up] / بِالضَّبْط, تَمَامًا (Without approximation; precisely.) / بِالْضَبْط (Signifies agreement or recognition.)  [exactly]",
 "それぞれ": "كُلّ (All; every; qualifying a singular noun, indicating all examples of the thing so )  [each]\nمثال: その兄弟はそれぞれ車を所有している。\n→ Each of the brothers has a car.",
 "それだから": "إِذَنْ, لِذٰلِكَ (Consequently, by or in consequence of that or this cause; referring to something)  [therefore]\nمثال: 自分が利口だと思ってもさしつかえないが、それだからと言って私をあざ笑うことはできないよ。\n→ You may think you are clever, but you cannot laugh at me because of that.",
 "それだけのかちがある": "اِسْتَحَقَّ (To earn, win.)  [deserving]\nمثال: その小説を読むことはそれだけの価値がある。\n→ It is worthwhile reading the novel.",
 "それだけの価値がある": "اِسْتَحَقَّ (To earn, win.)  [deserving]\nمثال: その小説を読むことはそれだけの価値がある。\n→ It is worthwhile reading the novel.",
 "それっぽい": "هَٰكَذَا, كَذَا (Used adverbially or adjectivally to indicate similitude, similarity, equivalent )  [(something) like that]\nمثال: チャットルームで知り合った人をパブで探したが、それっぽい人はいなかった。\n→ I searched at the pub for the person I had met online, but there was nobody who looked like that. / أَقْنَعَ (To make someone believe, or feel sure about something, especially by using logic)  [convincing]",
 "それで": "فَـ, لِذَا (As a result; for that reason; therefore; because of this; due to this.) / إِذًا, فَ (Used after a pause for thought to introduce a new topic, question or story, or a)  [so]\nمثال: 雨がひどく降ってきた、それで私たちは屋内で遊んだ。\n→ It was raining hard, so we played indoors.",
 "それでは": "[well, ... ; right, ...]\nused to end a conversation or introduce a remark / فَـ, لِذَا (As a result; for that reason; therefore; because of this; due to this.) / إِذًا, فَ (Used after a pause for thought to introduce a new topic, question or story, or a)  [so]\nمثال: それでは私の立つ瀬がない。\n→ That would leave me in a fix. / [that way (would mean ...) ; if that is the case] / [bye then]",
 "それでも": "لٰكِن, لٰكِنَّ (However, although, nevertheless, on the other hand (introducing a clause contrar) / لٰكِن, وَلٰكِنْ (On the contrary, rather (as a regular adversative conjunction, introducing a wor) / إِلَّا, سِوًى (Except that (introducing a subordinate clause which qualifies a negative stateme) / إلَّا, غَيْرَ (Only; solely; merely.)  [but (still)]\nمثال: 雨が激しく降っていますそれでも私は行かなければならない。\n→ It's raining hard and yet I must go.",
 "それでもって": "وَـ (used to connect two similar words, phrases, et cetera) / وَ (used to string together sentences or sentence fragments in c)  [and (so)]\nمثال: オレ、教室で屁をこいちゃったんっすよ。んでもって先生に追い出されちゃって。\n→ I farted in class, and the teacher threw me out.",
 "それと": "أَيْضًا, كَذٰلِكَ (In addition; besides; as well; further; too.)  [also]\nمثال: それと俺がホモだとしたら、罪になるわけ？\n→ And if I were gay, would that be a crime?",
 "それとも": "أَو, أَم (An operator denoting the disjunction of two propositions or truth values. There )  [or]\nمثال: あなたはリンゴが好きですか、それともオレンジが好きですか。\n→ Do you like apples or oranges?",
 "それとわかる": "مَلْحُوظ (Capable of being seen or noticed.) / جَدِير بِالْمُلَاحَظَة (Worthy of note; significant.)  [noticeable]",
