 "たしなみ": "ذَوْق, طَعْم (One of the sensations produced by the tongue in response to certain chemicals; t) / ذَوْق (A person's implicit set of preferences, especially esthetic, though also culinar) / ذَاقَ, تَذَوَّقَ (To sample the flavor of something orally.) / ذَاقَ, تَذَوَّقَ (To experience.)  [taste (in goods, etc.)]\nمثال: 彼は金持ちだがたしなみがない。\n→ He has more money than taste. / أُسْلُوب, طَرِيقَة (Mode of action; way of performing or doing anything.)  [manners] / تَوَاضُع (The quality of being modest; having a limited and not overly high opinion of one) / حِشْمَة (Pudency, avoidance of sexual explicitness.)  [modesty] / تَنْفِيذ (The act of accomplishing; completion; fulfilment.)  [accomplishments]\nمثال: 大部分ではないにしても多くの人々が文学的趣味を優美なたしなみと見なしている。\n→ Many people, if not most, look on literary taste as an elegant accomplishment.",
 "たしなむ": "اِسْتَمْتَعَ, تَمَتَّعَ (To receive pleasure or satisfaction from something.) / حَظِيَ (To have the use or benefit of something.)  [to enjoy (in moderation)]\nمثال: 彼は時々ワインをたしなむが、たいていはウイスキーを飲む。\n→ He enjoys wine sometimes, but mostly he drinks whisky. / سَاعَة (A portable or wearable timepiece.) / حَارِس (A person or group of people who guard.) / رَصَدَ (To observe over a period of time; to notice or pay attention.) / حَذِرَ (To be wary or cautious of.) / حَرَسَ (To attend to dangers to or regarding.)  [to watch (e.g. one's behaviour)]",
 "たしなめる": "قَرَّعَ, وَبَّخَ (To admonish in blame; to reproach angrily.)  [to chide]\nمثال: 彼は彼女の不実をたしなめた。\n→ He chided her for her unfaithfulness.",
