 "たす": "جَمَعَ (To sum up; to put together mentally; to add up.) / أَضَافَ (To append (e.g. a statement); to say further information.) / أَضَافَ (To intensify; to augment; to increase.) / أَضَافَ (To add someone as a friend.)  [to add (numbers)]\nمثال: ６０にするためには１７に何を足せばよいの。\n→ What do you have to add to 17 to get 60? / جَمَعَ (To sum up; to put together mentally; to add up.) / أَضَافَ (To append (e.g. a statement); to say further information.) / أَضَافَ (To intensify; to augment; to increase.) / أَضَافَ (To add someone as a friend.)  [to add (something)]\nمثال: もしコーヒーが濃すぎれば、いくらかお湯を足して下さい。\n→ If the coffee is too strong, add some more water. / [to take care of (e.g. one's business)]",
 "たすう": "كَثِير (before a countable noun: A large, indefinite number of.) / كَثِير, متعدد (A large, indefinite number of people or things.)  [many]\nمثال: 会議は出席者多数だった。\n→ The meeting was attended by many. / غَالِبِيَّة, أَغْلَبِيّة (More than half (50%) of some group.)  [majority]\nمثال: 多数が彼に賛成だった。\n→ The majority was for him.",
