 "たたきだす": "[to begin to strike] / نَار, نار (An instance of this chemical reaction, especially when intentionally created and) / حَرِيق, حريجة (The occurrence, often accidental, of fire in a certain place, causing damage and) / طَرَدَ (To terminate the employment contract of (an employee), especially for cause (suc)  [to fire (someone)]\nمثال: 彼女はプラスチックの玩具のバットで大きな蛇をたたき出した。\n→ She beat off a big snake with a plastic toy bat. / [to hammer (pattern, etc.) into metal]",
 "たたきつける": "ضَرَبَ (To have a sharp or sudden physical effect, as of a blow.) / إِضْرَاب (A work stoppage (or otherwise concerted stoppage of an activity) as a form of pr)  [to strike]\nمثال: 彼は茶碗を床にたたきつけた。\n→ He dashed the cup on the floor. / [to thrust at someone (e.g. a letter)]",
 "たたきつぶす": "كَسَّرَ (To break (something brittle) violently.) / تَكَسَّرَ (To be destroyed by being smashed.)  [to smash] / هَرَسَ (To reduce to fine particles by pounding or grinding.)  [to crush (an opponent, hopes, etc.)]",
 "たたきのめす": "صَرَعَ (To hit or collide with)  [to knock down]\nمثال: 試合が始まれば、彼は初めからとばしていくだろうし、ルチアーノは簡単に叩きのめされてしまうだろう。\n→ When the bell rings, he'll start strong and Luciano will lose quickly.",
 "たたきふせる": "صَرَعَ (To hit or collide with)  [to knock down]",
 "たたきわる": "كَسَّرَ (To break (something brittle) violently.) / تَكَسَّرَ (To be destroyed by being smashed.)  [to smash]",
 "たたき上げ": "[working one's way up]\nمثال: 彼はいわゆるたたき上げだ。\n→ He is what we call a self-made man. / مُحَارِب قَدِيم (A person with long experience of a particular activity.)  [veteran]",
 "たたき付ける": "ضَرَبَ (To have a sharp or sudden physical effect, as of a blow.) / إِضْرَاب (A work stoppage (or otherwise concerted stoppage of an activity) as a form of pr)  [to strike]\nمثال: 彼は茶碗を床にたたきつけた。\n→ He dashed the cup on the floor. / [to thrust at someone (e.g. a letter)]",
 "たたき出す": "[to begin to strike] / نَار, نار (An instance of this chemical reaction, especially when intentionally created and) / حَرِيق, حريجة (The occurrence, often accidental, of fire in a certain place, causing damage and) / طَرَدَ (To terminate the employment contract of (an employee), especially for cause (suc)  [to fire (someone)]\nمثال: 彼女はプラスチックの玩具のバットで大きな蛇をたたき出した。\n→ She beat off a big snake with a plastic toy bat. / [to hammer (pattern, etc.) into metal]",
 "たたき割る": "كَسَّرَ (To break (something brittle) violently.) / تَكَسَّرَ (To be destroyed by being smashed.)  [to smash]",
 "たたく": "ضَرَبَ (To have a sharp or sudden physical effect, as of a blow.) / إِضْرَاب (A work stoppage (or otherwise concerted stoppage of an activity) as a form of pr)  [to strike]\nمثال: 見知らぬ人が玄関のドアをしきりにたたいた。\n→ A stranger beat urgently at the front door. / هُجُوم m هَجْمَة (attempt to cause damage, injury, or death) / حَمْلَة (attempt to cause damage, injury, or death) / هَاجَمَ (To apply violent force to someone or something.)  [to attack]\nمثال: 新聞は一斉にその政治家をたたきはじめた。\n→ The newspapers opened fire on the politician. / [to sound out (someone's views)] / بَاوْنْد (unit of mass (16 ounces avoirdupois)) / رَطْل (unit of mass (16 ounces avoirdupois)) / جُنَيْه (unit of currency) / لِيرَة f or لَيْرَة (unit of currency)  [to pound (meat or fish)]",
 "たたす": "رَفَعَ (to cause to rise)  [to raise]",
 "たたずまい": "ظُهُور (The act of appearing or coming into sight; the act of becoming visible to the ey) / مَظْهَر (A thing seen; a phenomenon; an apparition.) / مَظْهَر, شَكْل (The way something looks; personal presence) / شَكْل (Apparent likeness; the way which something or someone appears to others.)  [appearance]",
