 "たたっ切る": "اِخْتَرَقَ (To gain unauthorized access to a computer or online account belonging to (a pers) / حيلة (A trick, shortcut, skill, or novel method to increase productivity, efficiency, )  [to hack]\nmore emphatic than 叩き切る",
 "たたっ斬る": "اِخْتَرَقَ (To gain unauthorized access to a computer or online account belonging to (a pers) / حيلة (A trick, shortcut, skill, or novel method to increase productivity, efficiency, )  [to hack]\nmore emphatic than 叩き切る",
 "たたみかける": "آلَةُ طِبَاعَة, آلَةُ الطِّبَاعَة (A printing machine.) / صِحَافَة, صَحَافَة (The print-based media (both the people and the newspapers).) / ضَغَطَ (To drive or thrust by pressure, to force in a certain direction.)  [to press (for an answer, etc.)]",
 "たたみこむ": "[to fold in ; to fold up] / ذَكَرَ, حَفِظَ (To hold (something) in the memory; to remember; also, to be mindful of or pay at)  [to bear in mind] / [to do in rapid succession ; to do relentlessly]",
 "たたみめ": "طَوَى (To bend (any thin material, such as paper) over so that it comes in contact with) / طَيَّة (That which is folded together, or which enfolds or envelops.)  [fold] / [mesh of a tatami mat ; distance between stitches in a tatami mat]",
 "たたみ込む": "[to fold in ; to fold up] / ذَكَرَ, حَفِظَ (To hold (something) in the memory; to remember; also, to be mindful of or pay at)  [to bear in mind] / [to do in rapid succession ; to do relentlessly]",
 "たたむ": "طَوَى (To bend (any thin material, such as paper) over so that it comes in contact with) / طَيَّة (That which is folded together, or which enfolds or envelops.)  [to fold (clothes, umbrella)]\nمثال: 彼女はタオルをきれいにたたみ、それを物入れに仕舞った。\n→ She folded up the towels and put them away in the cupboard. / أَغْلَقَ, سَكَّر (To remove or block an opening, gap or passage through.) / قَرِيب (Having little difference or distance in place, position, or abstractly; see also)  [to close (a shop, business)]\nمثال: 彼は商売をたたんで引退した。\n→ He sold his business and retired. / أخْلَا (To move out of a dwelling or other property, either by choice or by eviction.) / تَرَكَ (To leave an office or position.) / أبْطَلَ, نَحّى (To have a court judgement set aside; to annul.)  [to vacate]",
 "たたり": "لَعْنَة (A supernatural detriment or hindrance; a bane.) / لَعْنَة (A prayer or imprecation that harm may befall someone.) / نِقْمَة (The cause of great harm, evil, or misfortune; that which brings evil or severe a) / لَعَنَ (To place a curse upon (a person or object).) / لَعَنَ (To call upon divine or supernatural power to send injury upon; to imprecate evil) / شَتَمَ, سَبَّ (To use offensive or morally inappropriate language.)  [curse]\nمثال: 後のたたりが恐いぞ。\n→ There will be the deuce to pay.",
 "たたりめ": "بَلَاء, بُؤْس (An event resulting in great loss.)  [calamity]\nusu. as 弱り目に～\nمثال: 弱り目に祟り目。\n→ Misfortunes never come singly.",
 "たたり目": "بَلَاء, بُؤْس (An event resulting in great loss.)  [calamity]\nusu. as 弱り目に～\nمثال: 弱り目に祟り目。\n→ Misfortunes never come singly.",
 "たたる": "لَعْنَة (A supernatural detriment or hindrance; a bane.) / لَعْنَة (A prayer or imprecation that harm may befall someone.) / نِقْمَة (The cause of great harm, evil, or misfortune; that which brings evil or severe a) / لَعَنَ (To place a curse upon (a person or object).) / لَعَنَ (To call upon divine or supernatural power to send injury upon; to imprecate evil) / شَتَمَ, سَبَّ (To use offensive or morally inappropriate language.)  [to curse]\nمثال: 触らぬ神に祟りなし。\n→ Let sleeping dogs lie. / [to cause a bad result ; to bring about a negative outcome]",
 "ただ": "عَادِيّ, مَأْلُوف (Being part of the natural order of things; normal, customary, routine.)  [ordinary]\nمثال: 私はただの名無しの権兵衛です。\n→ I am just a nobody. / مَجَّانِيّ, مَجَّانًا (Not requiring any payment.)  [free of charge]\nesp. 只 if written with kanji\nمثال: 私はその切符をただで手にいれた。\n→ I got the ticket for nothing. / كَمَا هُوَ, كَمَا هِيَ (as it is; in its present unchangeable state or condition, especially as a contra)  [as is]\nusu. as ～では...\nمثال: 彼は結構しぶといね。転んでもただでは起きぬ、いい根性しているよ。\n→ He's a tenacious guy who always manages to come out on top. He's the kind of guy who can turn any situation to his advantage. / وَحِيد (1. alone in a category) / فَقَط (Without others or anything further; exclusively.) / فَقَط (No more than; just.) / فَقَط (Introduces a clause with negative polarity, often one which upsets the listener')  [only]\nمثال: 君はただ皿を洗いさえすればいい。\n→ All you have to do is wash the dishes.",
 "ただい": "رَائِع, عَظِيم (Very good; excellent; wonderful; fantastic.) / عَظِيم, كَبِير (Doing or exemplifying (a characteristic or pursuit) on a large scale; active or )  [great (quantity, amount, etc.)]\nمثال: 台風は多大の被害を与えた。\n→ The typhoon has done much harm.",
 "ただいま": "[I'm home! ; I'm back!]\nمثال: ただいま、お母さん。\n→ I'm home, Mom! / الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now]\nمثال: 申し訳ありませんが、ただ今満室になっています。\n→ I'm afraid we're quite full at the moment. / آنِفاً (Very close to the present moment; just a moment ago.)  [just now]\nمثال: メアリーはただいま戻ったところです。\n→ Mary has just come home. / حَالاً (Immediately; now; right away.)  [at once]\nمثال: ただいま参ります。\n→ I will be with you right away.",
 "ただこと": "كَلَام مُبَاشِر, مُقْتَبَس (The verbatim representation of a speaker's words, usually enclosed in quotation )  [direct speech]",
 "ただごと": "كَلَام مُبَاشِر, مُقْتَبَس (The verbatim representation of a speaker's words, usually enclosed in quotation )  [direct speech]",
 "たださえ": "قَد, مِنْ قَبْلُ (Prior to some specified time, either past, present, or future; by this time; pre) / لقد (So soon.)  [already]",
 "ただし": "لٰكِن, لٰكِنَّ (However, although, nevertheless, on the other hand (introducing a clause contrar) / لٰكِن, وَلٰكِنْ (On the contrary, rather (as a regular adversative conjunction, introducing a wor) / إِلَّا, سِوًى (Except that (introducing a subordinate clause which qualifies a negative stateme) / إلَّا, غَيْرَ (Only; solely; merely.)  [but]\nمثال: ただし、列をつくって並ばなくてはならないが・・・。\n→ However, you have to queue...",
 "ただしい": "يَمِين, يمين (Clockwise, particularly when describing a change in direction or orientation.) / صَحِيح, صَوَاب (Complying with justice, correctness, or reason; correct, just, true. See also th) / قَائِم (Of an angle, measuring 90 degrees, or one quarter of a complete rotation; the an) / عَلَى اَلْيَمِين (On the right side.) / إِلَى اَلْيَمِين (Towards the right side.) / صحيح, تمام (Yes, that is correct; I agree.) / حَقّ, حُقُوق (A legal, just or moral entitlement.) / يَمِين (A wave breaking from right to left (viewed from the shore).) / صَحَّحَ (To correct.)  [right]\nمثال: これが正しいかどうか自信がないんだ。\n→ I'm not sure if this is correct. / صَالِح (Free from sin or guilt.) / صَالِح (Moral and virtuous, perhaps to the point of sanctimony.) / صَالِح (Justified morally.)  [righteous]",
 "ただしく": "يَمِين, يمين (Clockwise, particularly when describing a change in direction or orientation.) / صَحِيح, صَوَاب (Complying with justice, correctness, or reason; correct, just, true. See also th) / قَائِم (Of an angle, measuring 90 degrees, or one quarter of a complete rotation; the an) / عَلَى اَلْيَمِين (On the right side.) / إِلَى اَلْيَمِين (Towards the right side.) / صحيح, تمام (Yes, that is correct; I agree.) / حَقّ, حُقُوق (A legal, just or moral entitlement.) / يَمِين (A wave breaking from right to left (viewed from the shore).) / صَحَّحَ (To correct.)  [right]",
 "ただしつき": "شَرْطِيّ (Stating that one sentence is true if another is true.)  [conditional]",
 "ただしづき": "شَرْطِيّ (Stating that one sentence is true if another is true.)  [conditional]",
 "ただす": "سَأَلَ, سأل (To request or petition.)  [to ask (about)]",
 "ただただ": "مطلقا, على الإطلاق (In an absolute or unconditional manner; utterly, positively, wholly.)  [absolutely]\nemphatic form of ただ\nمثال: 母はただただ泣くだけだった。\n→ My mother did nothing but weep.",
 "ただちに": "حَالاً (Immediately; now; right away.)  [at once]\nمثال: 我々は直ちにこの問題に対処しなければならない。\n→ We should deal with this matter without delay. / مُبَاشَرَةً (In a direct manner; in a straight line or course.)  [directly (face, lead to, etc.)]",
 "ただでさえ": "قَد, مِنْ قَبْلُ (Prior to some specified time, either past, present, or future; by this time; pre) / لقد (So soon.)  [already]",
 "ただでは": "[having serious consequences ; costing dearly]\nabbr. of ～すまない or ～おかない / مَجَّانًا, بلاش (Without paying; free.)  [for free]\nusu. followed by a negative verb",
 "ただなか": "مُنْتَصَف, وَسَط (A centre, midpoint.) / وَسَط, مُتَوَسْط (Located in the middle; in between.)  [middle] / فِي مُنْتَصَف, وَسْطَ (Among, in the middle of; amidst.)  [midst (e.g. of a storm)]",
 "ただならない": "جِدِّيّ (Without humor or expression of happiness; grave in manner or disposition.) / جَدِّيّ, جَادّ (Important; weighty; not insignificant.) / جَدِّيّ, جَادّ (Really intending what is said (or planned, etc); in earnest; not jocular or dece)  [serious] / [incomparable]\nمثال: さすがは、王子様ですわね。きっとただならない傑物の素質をお持ちなのですわ。\n→ Isn't that just what you'd expect from the prince? He certainly has the character of a truly great man.",
 "ただならぬ": "اِسْتِثْنَائِيّ, غَيْرُ عَادِيّ (Out of the ordinary; exceptional; unusual.)  [extraordinary]",
 "ただに": "بِالْكَاد (Without any other reason etc.; only, just, and nothing more.)  [merely]",
 "ただのいちども": "يَوْمًا (At any time.)  [(not) ever]\nwith neg. verb",
 "ただの一度も": "يَوْمًا (At any time.)  [(not) ever]\nwith neg. verb",
 "ただひとつ": "وَحِيد (Only.) / عَزْب (Unmarried (especially of a woman); widowed.) / أَخْمُص, بَاطِن القَدَم (The bottom or plantar surface of the foot.) / نَعْل (The bottom of a shoe or boot.) / سَمَك مُوسَى (Solea solea, a flatfish of the family Soleidae; a true sole.)  [sole]\nمثال: ただ一つの方法は、彼女に助けを求めることだった。\n→ The only way was to ask her for help.",
 "ただよう": "طَفَا, عَامَ (To be supported by a fluid of greater density (than the object).) / طَفَا (To be capable of floating.)  [to float]\nمثال: この無限の空間に漂う永遠の沈黙が私を恐怖に陥れる。\n→ The eternal silence of these infinite spaces terrifies me. / [to waft (e.g. a scent) ; to hang in the air] / [to be in the air (e.g. a feeling or mood)] / تَجَوَّلَ (To move without purpose or specified destination; often in search of livelihood.)  [to wander]",
 "ただれ": "مُوجِع, مُؤْلِم (Causing pain or discomfort; painfully sensitive.) / سَعْفَة (An injured, infected, inflamed or diseased patch of skin.)  [sore]",
 "ただれる": "تَقَيَّحَ (To become septic; to become rotten.)  [to fester] / [to be dissipated ; to be dissolute]",
 "ただ一つ": "وَحِيد (Only.) / عَزْب (Unmarried (especially of a woman); widowed.) / أَخْمُص, بَاطِن القَدَم (The bottom or plantar surface of the foot.) / نَعْل (The bottom of a shoe or boot.) / سَمَك مُوسَى (Solea solea, a flatfish of the family Soleidae; a true sole.)  [sole]\nمثال: ただ一つの方法は、彼女に助けを求めることだった。\n→ The only way was to ask her for help.",
 "ただ今": "[I'm home! ; I'm back!]\nمثال: ただいま、お母さん。\n→ I'm home, Mom! / الْآنَ, حَالًا (At the present time.) / بِمَا أَنّ, أَمَا وَأَنّ (Since, because, in light of the fact.)  [now]\nمثال: 申し訳ありませんが、ただ今満室になっています。\n→ I'm afraid we're quite full at the moment. / آنِفاً (Very close to the present moment; just a moment ago.)  [just now]\nمثال: メアリーはただいま戻ったところです。\n→ Mary has just come home. / حَالاً (Immediately; now; right away.)  [at once]\nمثال: ただいま参ります。\n→ I will be with you right away.",
 "たち": "جَرَحَ (To incise, to cut into the surface of something.) / قَصَّ (To remove (text, a picture, etc.) and place in memory in order to paste at a lat)  [cut]",
 "たちあい": "حُضُور (The fact or condition of being present, or of being within sight or call, or at )  [presence (e.g. of an observer)] / [trading session (at an exchange)] / [rising from a crouch to charge ; initial charge]\nesp. 立ち合い",
 "たちあいにん": "شَهَادَة (Attestation of a fact or event; testimony.) / شَاهِد, شَاهِدَة (One who sees or has personal knowledge of something.) / شَاهِد, شَاهِدَة (Someone called to give evidence in a court.) / شَاهِد, شَوَاهِد (Something that serves as evidence; a sign or token.) / شَهِدَ (To see or gain knowledge of through experience.)  [witness]",
 "たちあう": "حَضَرَ ((''ambitransitive'') to be present at or regularly go to)  [to attend]",
 "たちあがり": "أُسْلُوب (manner of expression in writing or speech) / أُسْلُوب (manner of creating, doing, or presenting something, especial)  [styling]",
 "たちあがる": "قَامَ (To rise from a lying or sitting position.)  [to stand up]\nمثال: 突然若い女性が立ち上がった。\n→ Suddenly, a young woman stood up. / شُفِيَ, بَرِئَ (To get better, to regain health or prosperity.)  [to recover] / نَجْمَة, اِبْتِدَاء (The beginning of an activity.) / نَجْمَة (The beginning point of a race, a board game, etc.) / بَدَأَ (To begin, commence, initiate.)  [to start (doing)]\nمثال: 多くの消費者は消費税反対に立ち上がった。\n→ Many consumers rose up against the consumption tax. / [to rise (from a crouch) and make the initial charge]",
 "たちあげる": "نَجْمَة, اِبْتِدَاء (The beginning of an activity.) / نَجْمَة (The beginning point of a race, a board game, etc.) / بَدَأَ (To begin, commence, initiate.)  [to start (something)]\nمثال: あの会社もついにホームページを立ち上げたらしい。\n→ That company just put up a web page. / جَزْمَة (heavy shoe that covers part of the leg) / بسطار (heavy shoe that covers part of the leg)  [to boot (a computer)]\nمثال: ノートパソコンの電源を入れ、ブラウザを立ち上げて、もう覚えてしまったアドレスを打ち込む。\n→ I switch on my laptop, start up the browser, and type in the address I've already learnt by heart.",
 "たちい": "حَرَكَة (Physical motion between points in space.) / حَرَكَة (A trend in various fields or social categories, a group of people with a common )  [movements]",
 "たちいえ": "مَجْلِس (A building used for something other than a residence (typically with qualifying )  [house]",
 "たちいく": "آخِر (Final, ultimate, coming after all others of its kind.) / مَاضٍ, الْمَاضِي (Most recent, latest, last so far.) / آخر (after everything else; finally) / اِسْتَمَرَّ, دَامَ (To endure, continue over time.)  [to last]",
 "たちいたる": "بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [to reach]\nمثال: 彼はこれまでこんな苦境に立ち至ったことはなかった。\n→ Never in his life had he encountered such a dilemma.",
 "たちいち": "مَوْقِع, مَكَان (A place or location.) / مَنْصِب (A post of employment; a job.) / مَكَانَة, رُتْبَة (A status or rank.) / رَأْي, مَوْقِف (An opinion, stand, or stance.) / جِلْسَة, وَقْفَة (A posture.)  [position (where one is standing)] / مَوْقِع, مَكَان (A place or location.) / مَنْصِب (A post of employment; a job.) / مَكَانَة, رُتْبَة (A status or rank.) / رَأْي, مَوْقِف (An opinion, stand, or stance.) / جِلْسَة, وَقْفَة (A posture.)  [position]",
 "たちいふるまい": "حَرَكَة (Physical motion between points in space.) / حَرَكَة (A trend in various fields or social categories, a group of people with a common )  [movements]",
 "たちいり": "أَدْخَلَ (To cause to go (into), or to be received (into); to put in; to insert; to cause ) / أَدْخَلَ (To type (something) into a computer; to input.) / دَخَلَ (To go into or upon, as lands, and take actual possession of them.)  [entering]\nمثال: 部外者の立ち入りを禁ず。\n→ No outsiders are allowed to enter.",
 "たちいりきんし": "مَمْنُوع الدُّخُولُ (Used on signs to indicate that entry into the area where the sign is displayed i)  [No Entry]\non a sign\nمثال: この建物は、現在立ち入り禁止だ。\n→ This building is off limits now. / حَدَّ, حَدَّدَ (To restrain within boundaries; to limit; to confine)  [restricted]",
 "たちいる": "أَدْخَلَ (To cause to go (into), or to be received (into); to put in; to insert; to cause ) / أَدْخَلَ (To type (something) into a computer; to input.) / دَخَلَ (To go into or upon, as lands, and take actual possession of them.)  [to enter]\nمثال: 警察は彼の生活に立ち入って調べ上げた。\n→ The police raked through his life. / [to meddle (in) ; to interfere (in)] / [to go deeply (into an issue) ; to delve deeper (into)]",
 "たちうり": "جَوَّال, بَائِع مُتَجَوِّل (An itinerant seller of small goods.)  [peddler]",
 "たちおうじょう": "مَعْلِف, مُرَاح (A compartment for a single animal in a stable or cattle shed.) / بَسْطة (A small open-fronted shop, for example in a market, food court, etc.)  [stalling]\nمثال: 私は病院へ行く途中、交通渋滞にあって立ち往生してしまった。\n→ I was held up on my way to the hospital in a traffic jam. / [being stumped ; being in a dilemma]\nمثال: フランス語の先生は生徒の質問に立ち往生した。\n→ The French teacher was stumped by her student's question. / [dying while standing (and remaining standing) ; dying on one's feet]",
 "たちかえる": "عَادَ, رَجَعَ (To return to a place.)  [to come back (to)]\nمثال: 面倒なようでも、基本に立ち返って検討し直したらどうだろう。急がば回れ、というじゃない。\n→ It may seem like a hassle, but I think you ought to go back to the basics and start over. Haste makes waste they say.",
 "たちかた": "جَرَحَ (To incise, to cut into the surface of something.) / قَصَّ (To remove (text, a picture, etc.) and place in memory in order to paste at a lat)  [cut]",
 "たちがれ": "صَعَقَ ((intransitive) shrivel, droop, dry up)  [withered]",
 "たちきく": "تَنَصَّتَ, تَسَمَّعَ (To hear (intentionally) a conversation one is not intended to hear; to listen in)  [to eavesdrop]",
 "たちきる": "جَرَحَ (To incise, to cut into the surface of something.) / قَصَّ (To remove (text, a picture, etc.) and place in memory in order to paste at a lat)  [to cut (cloth, paper, etc.)] / جَذَبَ, قَطَعَ (To cut free.)  [to sever (ties)]\nمثال: あのグループとの関係は断ち切るべきだ。\n→ You should cut off your connections with that group. / قَطَعَ (To remove by cutting.)  [to cut off (a supply route, enemy's retreat, etc.)]",
 "たちぎえる": "خَرَجَ (To leave, especially a building.) / خَرَجَ (To leave one's abode to go to public places, especially for recreation or entert)  [to go out (of a fire, etc.)]\nمثال: ろうそくは立ち消えた。\n→ The candle has gone out. / [to fall through (of plans, etc.) ; to fizzle out]",
 "たちぎき": "تَنَصُّت, اِسْتِرَاق سَمْع (verbal noun of eavesdrop:) / تَنَصُّت (verbal noun of eavesdrop:)  [eavesdropping]\nمثال: あなたの話を立ち聞きするつもりはありませんでした。\n→ I didn't mean to eavesdrop on your talk.",
 "たちくず": "خُرْدَة (Discarded objects (especially metal) that may be dismantled to recover their con) / يتخلى, نبذ (To discard; to get rid of.) / شجار (to fight)  [scraps]",
 "たちくらみ": "دُوَار (The state of being dizzy; the sensation of instability.)  [dizziness (from standing up too fast)]\nمثال: 立ちくらみがします。\n→ I get dizzy spells when I stand up.",
 "たちげいこ": "بَرُوفَة (The practising of something which is to be performed before an audience, usually)  [rehearsal]",
 "たちこえる": "[to rise above ; to transcend] / فَاقَ, تَجَاوَزَ (To go beyond or exceed (something) in an adjudicative or literal sense.)  [to surpass] / خَرَجَ (To leave, especially a building.) / خَرَجَ (To leave one's abode to go to public places, especially for recreation or entert)  [to go out]",
 "たちこめる": "كفن (Especially, the dress for the dead; a winding sheet.)  [to shroud]\nمثال: 湖から霧が立ちこめてきた。\n→ The fog was rising from the lake.",
 "たちさがり": "نَخْر (Rot; any processes or result of organic matter being gradually decomposed, espec) / اضمحل (to deteriorate) / تضعضع (to deteriorate)  [decay (e.g. charge, signal)]",
 "たちさる": "تَرَكَ (To have a consequence or remnant.) / تَرَكَ, غَادَرَ (To depart; to separate from.) / إِجَازَة, عُطْلَة (Permission to be absent; time away from one's work.)  [to leave]\nمثال: 私は彼の墓を立ち去り難かった。\n→ I hesitated to leave his grave.",
 "たちづめ": "مَنْزِلَة, مَكَانَة (Position or reputation in society or a profession.)  [standing (for a long period of time)]\nمثال: バスに空席がなかったので、駅までずっと立ちづめだった。\n→ There being no vacant seats on the bus, I was kept standing all the way to the station.",
 "たちとまる": "وَقَفَ, تَوَقَّفَ (To cease moving.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to cease moving or progressing.) / تَوَقَّفَ, وَقَّف (To cease; to no longer continue.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to come to an end.) / مَوْقِف (A (usually marked) place where buses, trams or trains halt to let passengers get) / وَقْفَة (An action of stopping; interruption of travel.)  [to stop (in one's tracks)]\nمثال: 彼は立ち止まってポスターをのぞき込んだ。\n→ He paused to look at the poster.",
 "たちとり": "[person in charge of beheading (concluding a seppuku)] / جَلَّاد (An official person who carries out the capital punishment of a criminal.)  [executioner] / [rikishi carrying a sword who follows the yokozuna to the ring during his ring-entering ceremony]",
 "たちどころに": "حَالاً (Immediately; now; right away.)  [at once]\nمثال: 悪運続きという目にあったので、私の財産は、たちどころに、ついえさってしまった。\n→ Having hit a streak of bad luck, my fortune had gone to pot in no time.",
 "たちどまる": "وَقَفَ, تَوَقَّفَ (To cease moving.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to cease moving or progressing.) / تَوَقَّفَ, وَقَّف (To cease; to no longer continue.) / أَوْقَفَ, وَقَفَ (To cause (something) to come to an end.) / مَوْقِف (A (usually marked) place where buses, trams or trains halt to let passengers get) / وَقْفَة (An action of stopping; interruption of travel.)  [to stop (in one's tracks)]\nمثال: 彼は立ち止まってポスターをのぞき込んだ。\n→ He paused to look at the poster.",
 "たちどり": "[person in charge of beheading (concluding a seppuku)] / جَلَّاد (An official person who carries out the capital punishment of a criminal.)  [executioner] / [rikishi carrying a sword who follows the yokozuna to the ring during his ring-entering ceremony]",
 "たちなおり": "شِفَاء, تَعَافِي (A return to normal health.)  [recovery]",
 "たちなおる": "[to regain one's footing ; to get back on one's feet]\nمثال: ショックから立ち直りましたか。\n→ Have you recovered from the shock? / شُفِيَ, بَرِئَ (To get better, to regain health or prosperity.)  [to recover]",
 "たちならぶ": "خَطّ (The wire connecting one telegraphic station with another, a telephone or interne)  [to line]\n建ち並ぶ refers to buildings\nمثال: その通りに立ち並ぶ木々は春に美しい花を咲かせます。\n→ The trees that line the street have lovely blossoms in spring. / [to be equal to ; to be on a par with]",
 "たちのかせる": "أَجْلَى, طَرَدَ (To expel (one or more people) from their property; to force (one or more people))  [to evict]",
 "たちのき": "طَرْد (The act of evicting.)  [eviction]\nمثال: 立ち退きの予告を受けた。\n→ We received an eviction notice.",
 "たちのく": "تَرَكَ (To have a consequence or remnant.) / تَرَكَ, غَادَرَ (To depart; to separate from.) / إِجَازَة, عُطْلَة (Permission to be absent; time away from one's work.)  [to leave]\nمثال: 大水のため人々は立ち退いた。\n→ The people were evacuated because of the flood. / أخْلَا (To move out of a dwelling or other property, either by choice or by eviction.) / تَرَكَ (To leave an office or position.) / أبْطَلَ, نَحّى (To have a court judgement set aside; to annul.)  [to vacate]\nمثال: 彼は家賃をだいぶ滞納し、そのためアパートをたちのかされた。\n→ He was way behind on his rent. As a result, he was evicted from his apartment.",
 "たちのぼる": "نَهَضَ, اِرْتَفْعَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.) / أَشْرَقَ, شَرَقَ (To move, or appear to move, physically upwards relative to the ground.)  [to rise (of smoke, steam, etc.)]\nمثال: 彼は立ち上るように言われ、ゆっくりとそうした。\n→ He was told to stand up, and he did so slowly.",
 "たちば": "مَوْقِع, مَكَان (A place or location.) / مَنْصِب (A post of employment; a job.) / مَكَانَة, رُتْبَة (A status or rank.) / رَأْي, مَوْقِف (An opinion, stand, or stance.) / جِلْسَة, وَقْفَة (A posture.)  [position]\nمثال: お答えできる立場にありません。\n→ I'm not in a position to answer. / وِجْهَة نَظَر, حَيْثِيَّة (A position from which something is seen.) / وِجْهَة نَظَر (An attitude, opinion, or set of beliefs.)  [point of view]\nمثال: 彼女の立場からその問題をとらえるようにしなさい。\n→ Try to see the problem from her point of view.",
 "たちばん": "حَارِس, خَفِير (A sentry, watch, or guard.)  [sentinel]",
 "たちふるまい": "حَرَكَة (Physical motion between points in space.) / حَرَكَة (A trend in various fields or social categories, a group of people with a common )  [movements] / [farewell dinner (given by someone about to leave on a trip)]",
 "たちふるまう": "عَمَل (Something done, a deed.) / قَانُون ((In the United States) A legislative proposal, a bill that has not yet become la) / مَثَّلَ (To perform a theatrical role.) / تَصَرَّفَ (To behave in a certain manner for an indefinite length of time.)  [to act]",
 "たちぶるまい": "[farewell dinner (given by someone about to leave on a trip)]",
 "たちまさる": "فَاقَ, تَجَاوَزَ (To go beyond or exceed (something) in an adjudicative or literal sense.)  [to surpass]",
 "たちまじる": "وَصَلَ (To connect or combine into one; to put together.) / اِتَّصَلَ (To come together; to meet.) / اِلْتَحَقَ بِـ, اِنْضَمَّ إِلَى (To become a member of.)  [to join (a group)]",
 "たちまち": "فَوْرًا, حَالًا (In an immediate manner; instantly or without delay.)  [immediately]\nمثال: 切符はたちまち売り切れた。\n→ The tickets were sold out in a moment. / فَجْأَةً (Happening quickly and with little or no warning; in a sudden manner.)  [suddenly]",
 "たちまわり": "عَارَكَ, قَاتَلَ (Senses relating to physical conflict:) / تَعَارَكَ, تَقَاتَلَ (Senses relating to physical conflict:) / نَاضَلَ, كَافَحَ (To strive for something; to campaign or contend for success.) / قِتَال (An occasion of fighting.) / مَعْرَكَة (A battle between opposing armies.)  [fight] / [walking about ; walking around] / [conducting oneself] / تَجَوُّل, تَنَزُّه (A wandering on foot; an idle and leisurely walk; a ramble; a saunter.) / تَجَوَّلَ, تَنَزَّهَ (To wander on foot; to ramble idly or leisurely; to rove.)  [stroll (in noh, an action piece involving circling the stage)]",
 "たちまわる": "[to walk about ; to walk around] / عَمَل (Something done, a deed.) / قَانُون ((In the United States) A legislative proposal, a bill that has not yet become la) / مَثَّلَ (To perform a theatrical role.) / تَصَرَّفَ (To behave in a certain manner for an indefinite length of time.)  [to act] / [to stop by (somewhere; esp. of a criminal on the run) ; to drop by] / [to enact a fighting scene ; to brawl (in a play, film, etc.)]",
 "たちみきゃく": "مَعْرِض, صَالَةُ عَرْض (An institution, building, or room for the exhibition and conservation of importa)  [the gallery]",
 "たちむかう": "عَارَض (To attempt to stop the progression of; to resist or antagonize by physical means) / اِعْتَرَضَ (To object to.)  [to oppose]\nمثال: 彼女は自分の運命に立ち向かう覚悟ができていた。\n→ She was ready to face her fate.",
 "たちもどる": "رَجَعَ, عَادَ (To come or go back (to a place or person).) / أَرْجَعَ, أَعَادَ (To give something back to its original holder or owner.) / عَوْدَة (The act of returning.)  [to return]",
 "たちゆく": "آخِر (Final, ultimate, coming after all others of its kind.) / مَاضٍ, الْمَاضِي (Most recent, latest, last so far.) / آخر (after everything else; finally) / اِسْتَمَرَّ, دَامَ (To endure, continue over time.)  [to last]",
 "たちよみ": "تَصَفَّحَ, اِسْتَعْرَضَ (To scan, to casually look through in order to find items of interest, especially)  [browsing (i.e. reading an item but not buying it)]",
 "たちよる": "[to drop by ; to stop by]\nمثال: 夕方会社にお立ち寄りください。\n→ Drop by my office this evening. / اِقْتَرَبَ (To come or go near, in place or time; to move toward; to advance nearer; to draw) / اِقْتِرَاب, مُقَارَبَة (An act of drawing near in place or time; an advancing or coming near.) / كَيْفِيَّة, طَرِيقَة (A manner of making (a policy) or solving (a problem, etc.).)  [to approach]",
 "たちわる": "انفصل (To separate.)  [to split] / [to cut open]",
 "たちんぼ": "[streetwalker ; street girl] / [being kept standing (without doing anything) ; remaining on one's feet] / سَائِل (A person who begs.) / فَقِير (A person suffering from extreme poverty.)  [beggar] / [tout (for a hostess bar)]",
 "たちんぼう": "[streetwalker ; street girl] / [being kept standing (without doing anything) ; remaining on one's feet] / سَائِل (A person who begs.) / فَقِير (A person suffering from extreme poverty.)  [beggar] / [tout (for a hostess bar)]",
 "たっかーい": "عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:) / مَسْطُول (Intoxicated; under the influence of a mood-altering drug, formerly usually alcoh)  [high]\nمثال: 銀行はリスクの高い顧客へのローンには高い金利をつける。\n→ Banks charge higher interest on loans to risky customers. / غَالٍ, الْغَالِي (Having a high price or cost.)  [expensive]\nمثال: そんな高い車を買う余裕はありません。\n→ I can't afford to buy such an expensive car. / عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:) / مَسْطُول (Intoxicated; under the influence of a mood-altering drug, formerly usually alcoh)  [high (level)]\nمثال: 新しい製造過程は高い歩留まりを可能にする。\n→ The new production process achieves a high yield. / عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Noisy.)  [loud]",
 "たっきゅう": "بِينْغ بُونْغ, كُرَة طَاوِلَة (A game or sport (similar to tennis) that involves the hitting of a light plastic)  [table tennis]\nمثال: いくら年を取ってもまだ卓球をやる元気はある。\n→ No matter how old I get, I'll still have the energy to play ping-pong.",
 "たっけい": "صَلْب (execution by being nailed or tied to an upright cross)  [crucifixion]",
 "たっけん": "اِخْتِرَاقْ (act of penetrating)  [penetration]",
 "たっけー": "عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:) / مَسْطُول (Intoxicated; under the influence of a mood-altering drug, formerly usually alcoh)  [high]\nمثال: 銀行はリスクの高い顧客へのローンには高い金利をつける。\n→ Banks charge higher interest on loans to risky customers. / غَالٍ, الْغَالِي (Having a high price or cost.)  [expensive]\nمثال: そんな高い車を買う余裕はありません。\n→ I can't afford to buy such an expensive car. / عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Physically elevated, extending above a base or average level:) / مَسْطُول (Intoxicated; under the influence of a mood-altering drug, formerly usually alcoh)  [high (level)]\nمثال: 新しい製造過程は高い歩留まりを可能にする。\n→ The new production process achieves a high yield. / عَالٍ, اَلْعَالِي (Noisy.)  [loud]",
 "たっし": "إِشْعَار, إِخْطَار (The act of notifying.) / تَنْبِيه, إِشْعَار (A specific piece of information that serves to notify.)  [notification]\nمثال: 売れ行きは目標に達しなかった。\n→ Sales fell short of their goal.",
 "たっしき": "مَدَّ النَّظَرِ (The condition of being unable to focus on near objects; presbyopia.)  [farsightedness]",
 "たっしゃ": "صَحِيح, سَلِيم (Enjoying good health; free from disease or disorder.) / صِحِّيّ (Conducive to health.)  [healthy]\nمثال: 彼はとても年をとっているけれどたっしゃだ。\n→ Although he is very old, he is strong. / مَاهِر (Having or showing skill; skillful.)  [skilled]\nمثال: 彼女はフランス語が達者だ。\n→ She has a good command of French. / سَيِّد (Someone who has control over something or someone.) / سَيِّد (The owner of an animal or slave.) / أُصُولِيّ, أُصُولِيَّة (An expert at something.) / أحسن, أتقن (To learn to a high degree of proficiency.)  [master]",
 "たっす": "بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [to reach]",
 "たっする": "بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [to reach]\nمثال: 水は彼の腰の所まで達した。\n→ The water came up to his waist.",
 "たっせい": "إِنْجَاز (The act of achieving or performing; a successful performance; accomplishment.) / إِنْجَاز (A great or heroic deed or feat; something accomplished by valor or boldness.) / إِنْجَاز (An award for completing a particular task or meeting an objective in a video gam)  [achievement]\nمثال: アンは望んでいた目標を達成した。\n→ Ann has achieved her desired goal.",
 "たった": "وَحِيد (1. alone in a category) / فَقَط (Without others or anything further; exclusively.) / فَقَط (No more than; just.) / فَقَط (Introduces a clause with negative polarity, often one which upsets the listener')  [only]\nمثال: ここから歩いてたった１０分の距離です。\n→ It is no more than ten minutes' walk from here.",
 "たったいま": "آنِفاً (Very close to the present moment; just a moment ago.)  [just now]\nمثال: 時計がたった今十時を打った。\n→ The clock has just struck ten.",
 "たったひとつ": "أَحَادِيّ (Not accompanied by anything else; one in number.) / وَاحِد (Not divided in parts.) / أَعْزَب, غَيْر مُتَزَوِّج (Not married, and (in modern times) not dating or without a significant other.) / إصدار منفرد, أغنية منفردة (A popular song released and sold (on any format) nominally on its own though usu) / عَزَب (One who is not married or does not have a romantic partner.)  [single]",
 "たった一つ": "أَحَادِيّ (Not accompanied by anything else; one in number.) / وَاحِد (Not divided in parts.) / أَعْزَب, غَيْر مُتَزَوِّج (Not married, and (in modern times) not dating or without a significant other.) / إصدار منفرد, أغنية منفردة (A popular song released and sold (on any format) nominally on its own though usu) / عَزَب (One who is not married or does not have a romantic partner.)  [single]",
 "たった今": "آنِفاً (Very close to the present moment; just a moment ago.)  [just now]\nمثال: 時計がたった今十時を打った。\n→ The clock has just struck ten.",
 "たっち": "مَنْزِلَة, مَكَانَة (Position or reputation in society or a profession.)  [standing]",
 "たって": "بِالرَغْم مِن (Although; though; despite or in spite of the fact that.)  [even though]\nalso だって\nمثال: いまそれを直そうったって無駄だ。\n→ It's no use trying to fix it now. / [although one might say ; although called]\nalso ったって",
 "たっと": "قِيمَة (The quality that renders something desirable or valuable; worth.)  [value]",
 "たっとい": "ثَمِين (Of high value or worth.)  [precious]\nمثال: 愛より尊い物はない。\n→ Nothing is as precious as love. / نَبِيل, شريف (An aristocrat; one of aristocratic blood.) / كَرِيم, شَرِيف (Having honorable qualities; having moral eminence and freedom from anything pett)  [noble]",
 "たっとき": "ثَمِين (Of high value or worth.)  [precious] / نَبِيل, شريف (An aristocrat; one of aristocratic blood.) / كَرِيم, شَرِيف (Having honorable qualities; having moral eminence and freedom from anything pett)  [(the) noble]\noft. preceding a name or title",
 "たっとぶ": "قِيمَة (The quality that renders something desirable or valuable; worth.)  [to value]\nمثال: イギリス人は自由を尊ぶ国民である。\n→ The English set a high value on freedom. / اِحْتِرَام (Good opinion, honor, or admiration.) / اِعْتِبَار, صَدَد (A particular aspect, feature or detail of something.) / اِحْتَرَمَ (To have respect for.)  [to respect]",
