 "たまご": "بَيْضَة (An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, repti)  [eggs]\nمثال: 卵を一ダースづつつめなさい。\n→ Pack eggs in dozens. / بَيْضَة (An approximately spherical or ellipsoidal body produced by birds, insects, repti)  [(hen's) egg]\noft. 玉子 in cooking\nمثال: 卵は硬くゆでてください。\n→ Boil the eggs hard. / مُسْتَقْبَل (The time ahead; those moments yet to be experienced.) / مُسْتَقْبَلِيّ, مُسْتَقْبَل (Having to do with or occurring in the future.)  [future (lawyer, doctor, etc.)]\nas ...の卵\nمثال: 彼は医者の卵だ。\n→ He's a future doctor. / بِدَايَة (The act of doing that which begins anything; commencement of an action, state, o) / بِدَايَة (That which begins or originates something; the source or first cause.) / بِدَايَة (The initial portion of some extended thing.)  [beginning]",
 "たまごがら": "قَشْر الْبَيْضِ (object)  [eggshell]",
 "たまごのから": "قَشْر الْبَيْضِ (object)  [eggshell]",
 "たまごめ": "حِمْل (A burden; a weight to be carried.) / حِمْل (The electrical current or power delivered by a device.) / عَبَّأَ, شَحَنَ (To put a load on or in (a means of conveyance or a place of storage).)  [loading (a gun)] / [loaded gun]",
 "たまごやき": "[rolled egg ; rolled omelette (omelet)] / بَيْض مَقْلِيّ (An egg that has been shallow-fried on one or both sides without being beaten or )  [fried egg] / [frying pan for making rolled eggs]",
 "たまさか": "صُدْفَةً, بِصُدْفَة (Unexpectedly, accidentally; without foreplanning.)  [by chance] / قَلِيلًا, قَلِيلًا مَا (Not occurring at a regular interval; seldom; not often.)  [rarely]",
 "たましい": "رُوح, نَفْس (The spirit or essence of a person usually thought to consist of one's thoughts a) / سول (Soul music.)  [soul]\nمثال: 魂の吐息を感じ始めた。\n→ I'm feeling the breath of life. / [willpower ; vitality] / [something as important as one's own life ; something invaluable] / [inherent spirit of something ; state of mind]\nusu. as ～だましい",
